    "summary": "A man&#039;s shirt made of natural cream tabby linen cloth.  Single length of cloth used centre front and back [full weaving width circa 39 cms].  Another full weaving width used at each side, together with four additional panels, creating an A-line shape.  Slit neckline (large linen panel inside) with applied red tabby cotton cloth decorated with white and green glass (?) beads grouped in threes, with one group of yellow beads. Sleeves set in at right angles.  Large diamond-shaped gusset under arms; made from red tabby linen cloth.  Outline of symmetrical stylized leaf motif embroidered in chain stitch, using cream linen thread.  Shirt very dirty and stained.",
